 "C0": {
  "code": "INELIG",
  "loc": "Abstract, p.1; Section 2, p.4",
  "quote": "This paper studies aggregation of preferences under ignorance",
  "note": "The main object is single-profile, Harsanyi-type aggregation of individual preferences over probability possibility sets into a social ranking. The results are Pareto/dictatorship and utilitarian representation theorems. There is no voting procedure, ballot or rule mapping submitted inputs to a collective decision, and no strategic or computational aspects of such a procedure. It is welfare-economic preference aggregation, not voting. This is a borderline call: AX-type social choice, but not 'by voting'."
 },
